INT. FLORESCENT BREAK ROOM - MERIDIAN SYNERGY CORP - DAY

A microwave beeps. A motivational poster reads TEAMWORK in a font that has given up.

A YOUNG WOMAN in a lanyard stands before the coffee machine, holding two empty pods and one full one. She has the posture of someone who has been told not to touch anything.

MS. VOLKOV, 50s, regional director, enters in a pencil skirt and a visible air of purpose.

MS. VOLKOV
You're the intern.

YOUNG WOMAN
Yes. Cassandra.

MS. VOLKOV
Cassandra. You've been here three weeks and I haven't seen you do one thing.

CASSANDRA
I've been doing the thing you asked.

MS. VOLKOV
What thing?

CASSANDRA
Shadowing you.

Ms. Volkov considers this. She takes the pod from Cassandra, studies it, and drops it in the trash.

MS. VOLKOV
Then she should have noticed I don't drink this brand.

CASSANDRA
She did.

MS. VOLKOV
Who?

CASSANDRA
Me. I noticed. I just didn't know she was allowed to say it.

They look at each other. The microwave beeps again.

MS. VOLKOV
You're promoted.

CASSANDRA
I'm what?

MS. VOLKOV
To associate. Effective now. She who notices things should be in the meetings.

CASSANDRA
Wait. Who is "she"?

MS. VOLKOV
(already leaving)
Whoever's holding the pod.

She exits. Cassandra looks down at the pod. Looks at the poster. Quietly, she sets the pod on the counter and walks out after her.
